[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:15.442 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Wow. Just from --

00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:18.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just from Fran Drescher
playing my mom, yeah.

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:19.879 line:92%
-You have three children.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:20.613 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-I have three children.

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:22.615 size:75% position:38%
-And you raised them
for a bit in L.A.,

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now you're raising the
in New York.

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:26.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
What's the difference like
for you?

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:28.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you have kids
in New York.

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:31.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I feel like
now I have to do things

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:33.393 size:75% position:38%
to, like, guard them
from the elements,

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:36.229
prepare them, you know, that
it's going to be cold outside.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:38.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they don't want
to even deal with that.

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:39.899
-Yeah.
-Because they have lived in L.A.

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:42.001
And so, in L.A., I'd be like
"It's a little cold outside.

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.137
You might want to wear
a jacket." They'd be like, "No."

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:46.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd be like, "Alright.
I don't care."

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now I'm like,
"It's cold outside.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
You want to put on a jacket?
And they're like, "No."

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:51.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm like,
"Alright. Suit yourself."

00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:53.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then as soon as we
get outside, they're like,

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.281 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"It's freezing!

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:57.117 line:92%
Why would you do this to me?!"

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:59.219
I'm like, "You -- Alright,
I'll go get you a jacket."

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:00.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I go get the jacket,
and I come back.

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:03.423
I'm like, "You want the jacket?"
They're like, "No!"

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:05.625 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What am I doing?

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:06.759 line:92%
But there's a lot more of that

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:08.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, seems like a part of it
that it's worse.

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:11.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then they get bossy
'cause they are New Yorkers.

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:13.633
-Yeah. Well, yes.
Now they tell everybody, like --

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:18.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
My son loves to go, "You kno
the water here? Amazing."

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:20.240 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
